msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 3.0 is the result of a lot of work and dedication from the community."
" Quarkus continues to be an Open Source stack to write Java applications "
"offering unparalleled startup time, memory footprint, and developer "
"experience."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The development of Quarkus 3 started last year on March 18, 2022, with the "
"crazy idea\n"
"that we could rewrite the whole tree to migrate to the new `jakarta.*` "
"packages\n"
"while continuing the development of Quarkus 2."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 3.0 is based on Jakarta EE 10 and, as you can expect,\n"
"it is not the only change. This version comes packed with new features and "
"enhancements\n"
"that we implemented during this period."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This announcement contains a lot of information about the new features and "
"how to upgrade\n"
"so we recommend reading it thoroughly before upgrading to Quarkus 3."
msgstr ""

msgid "New Dev UI"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 2 introduced the Dev UI, which provides a web UI to use during "
"development.\n"
"Extensions could provide their own Dev UI pages to provide additional "
"functionality."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 3.0 now has a new Dev UI that is more extensible and easier to use.\n"
"It also has a new and much-improved look and feel."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The new Dev UI is available by default. However,\n"
"because not all the extensions have migrated to the new Dev UI,\n"
"you can still access the old one at `/q/dev-v1`.\n"
"The old Dev UI is planned for removal in a future version."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We have a https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sz5ihmA4gaE&list="
"PLsM3ZE5tGAVbyncLm7ue2V25cwFck7ew9[playlist] on Quarkus YouTube channel that "
"shows off the new Dev UI, explains the new features and how to use and "
"extend it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Jakarta EE 10"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 2 was based on Jakarta EE 8. Quarkus 3 is based on Jakarta EE 10."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The most visible change is that the `javax.\\*` packages from Jakarta EE "
"have been moved to `jakarta.*`. This change requires changing any source "
"code and dependency and its transitive dependencies that rely on the `javax."
"*` packages."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"See the <<upgrading>> section for more information on how `quarkus update` "
"helps you migrate."
msgstr ""

msgid "The change to target Jakarta EE 10 brings two major improvements:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The broader Java ecosystem is moving to Jakarta dependencies, allowing for "
"easier sharing and compatible implementations."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"CDI introduces the notion of CDI Lite and Build Compatible Extensions (BCE), "
"which enable standard extensions that are compatible across CDI "
"implementations and reap the benefits of Quarkus build time optimizations."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Only the `javax.\\*` packages from Jakarta EE have changed.\n"
"The ones from the JDK are still under `javax.*`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Eclipse MicroProfile 6"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Eclipse MicroProfile 6.0 aligns with Jakarta EE 10 Core Profile and replaces "
"MicroProfile OpenTracing with MicroProfile Telemetry."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hibernate ORM 6"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One of the biggest changes in Quarkus 3 is that we upgraded Hibernate ORM "
"from version 5 to version 6.2."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hibernate ORM 6 is a new major release, and it comes with many changes,\n"
"some of them breaking."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To learn more about the changes in Hibernate ORM 6 from a Quarkus user "
"perspective, see https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-3."
"0:-Hibernate-ORM-5-to-6-migration[Hibernate ORM 5 to 6 migration]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Hibernate ORM release announcements have a lot of information about the "
"changes/improvements in Hibernate ORM 6:"
msgstr ""

msgid "https://in.relation.to/2022/03/31/orm-60-final/[Hibernate ORM 6.0]"
msgstr ""

msgid "https://in.relation.to/2022/06/14/orm-61-final/[Hibernate ORM 6.1]"
msgstr ""

msgid "https://in.relation.to/2023/03/30/orm-62-final/[Hibernate ORM 6.2]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Upgrading to Hibernate ORM 6 will require some effort and testing. Make sure "
"you have a look at the <<upgrading>> section below."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Some improvements have also been made to the Quarkus Hibernate ORM extension "
"itself, such as:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Support for `StatementInspector` as `@PersistenceUnitExtension` managed bean."
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The ability to inject a https://docs.jboss.org/hibernate/orm/6.2/userguide/"
"html_single/Hibernate_User_Guide.html#_statelesssession[`StatelessSession`] "
"by using CDI (Contexts and Dependency Injection)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hibernate Reactive 2"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hibernate Reactive has been upgraded to version 2.0 to be compatible with "
"Hibernate ORM 6."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mutiny 2 and Java Flow"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus was upgraded to https://smallrye.io/smallrye-mutiny/2.0.0/reference/"
"migrating-to-mutiny-2/[Mutiny 2]\n"
"and now uses the Java Flow API instead of Reactive Streams."
msgstr ""

msgid "Development Tools"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Developer experience is a key aspect of Quarkus, and we are constantly "
"improving it."
msgstr ""

msgid "CLI plugins"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Quarkus CLI is now extensible with plugins. See details in the https://"
"quarkus.io/version/main/guides/cli-tooling#extending-the-cli[CLI guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Expect many new features in the Quarkus CLI in the form of plugins in the "
"near future."
msgstr ""

msgid "Update tool"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 3.0 has a new update tool that radically simplifies updating your "
"projects to the latest version of Quarkus."
msgstr ""

msgid "You can learn more about it in the <<upgrading>> section."
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>quarkus deploy</code> in all dev tools"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus CLI and the Maven and Gradle plugins now have the ability to "
"`deploy` Quarkus applications."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This enables the deployment of Quarkus applications to platforms like "
"Kubernetes, Knative, and OpenShift.\n"
"All without requiring changes to the project dependencies or configuration, "
"simplifying developer experience."
msgstr ""

msgid "Support for Maven 3.9"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Maven 3.9 brought some breaking changes, and the integration with Quarkus "
"was not working properly.\n"
"It is now fixed and you can use Maven 3.9 to build your Quarkus 3 "
"applications."
msgstr ""

msgid "Also Maven 3.8.2 is the minimal requirement for Quarkus 3 projects."
msgstr ""

msgid "Gradle 8"
msgstr ""

msgid "Our Gradle support has been upgraded to Gradle 8."
msgstr ""

msgid "Management network interface"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Until now, all the Quarkus endpoints were exposed on the same network "
"interface."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Starting with Quarkus 3.0, you can expose technical endpoints such as the "
"health and metrics on a different interface thanks to link:/guides/"
"management-interface-reference[a specific management interface]."
msgstr ""

msgid "/q/info"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To expose information about your application (such as the git hash), add the "
"`quarkus-info` extension to your project."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The endpoint is available on `/q/info` and will be exposed on the management "
"network interface if you enable it."
msgstr ""

msgid "RESTEasy Reactive"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Many usability enhancements have come into RESTEasy Reactive, such as "
"retrieving all multipart parts."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Remember that RESTEasy Reactive is our default REST layer covering both "
"reactive and blocking workloads."
msgstr ""

msgid "OpenTelemetry"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The OpenTelemetry extension has been rewritten to support the SDK "
"autoconfiguration and went through many changes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The configuration namespace has changed to `quarkus.otel.*`. We recommend "
"switching to the new configuration properties, even though the old ones are "
"still supported for now."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Also, enabling OpenTelemetry for JDBC is now as simple as setting `quarkus."
"datasource.jdbc.telemetry` to `true`.\n"
"You don't have to modify your JDBC connection URL anymore."
msgstr ""

msgid "Multiple mailers"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sending emails via multiple SMTP servers is supported in Quarkus 3.0."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Have a look at the https://quarkus.io/version/main/guides/mailer-"
"reference#multiple-mailer-configurations[updated documentation]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Qute"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Qute, our templating engine, also got a lot of love with several new "
"features, such as the ability to cache a section of the template that rarely "
"changes thanks to link:/guides/qute-reference#cached-section[cached "
"sections]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Cache"
msgstr ""

msgid "It is now possible to use a Redis backend with the Cache extension."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information, see the https://quarkus.io/version/main/guides/cache-"
"redis-reference[dedicated guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The cache extension also allows you to define a global default cache "
"configuration that will be applied to all your caches."
msgstr ""

msgid "Database migrations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your database migrations with Flyway and Liquibase are now run as init "
"containers in manifests."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The notion of migration/setup work being done in init containers is "
"available for other extensions to implement and support."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Flyway extension supports custom credentials/URLs to connect to the "
"database\n"
"and you can more easily customize the configuration of the Flyway instance."
msgstr ""

msgid "MongoDB"
msgstr ""

msgid "``CredentialsProvider``s are now supported for MongoDB connections."
msgstr ""

msgid "Elasticsearch Java Client extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The new Elasticsearch Java Client is supported as a brand-new extension.\n"
"This solves the licensing problems that prevented us from updating the "
"deprecated High Level REST Client."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To use this new client, have a look at the updated link:/guides/"
"elasticsearch[Elasticsearch guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "gRPC"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Several enhancements have been made to the gRPC extensions, such as the "
"support of `InProcess`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Scheduler API"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can now schedule jobs programmatically by using the Scheduler "
"programmatic API,\n"
"described in the link:/guides/scheduler-"
"reference#programmatic_scheduling[Scheduler reference guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Kubernetes Client"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Kubernetes Client has been upgraded to version 6.5."
msgstr ""

msgid "Azure Functions extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The development of Azure functions is easier than ever, thanks to the new "
"Azure Functions extension."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Learn more about it in the link:/guides/azure-functions[dedicated guide]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Other changes"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus Platform readiness"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We have been working hard to make sure that the Quarkus Platform is ready "
"for production use.\n"
"Not every extension found in Quarkus 2 Platform is available or not yet "
"final in Quarkus 3 Platform yet, but they are on their way."
msgstr ""

msgid "The following extensions are available:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Debezium"
msgstr ""

msgid "Optaplanner"
msgstr ""

msgid "Google Cloud Services"
msgstr ""

msgid "Cassandra"
msgstr ""

msgid "Camel (M1 milestone)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The following extensions are not yet available, but will be available soon:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Operator SDK"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are using an extension that is missing or not working, please open "
"issues in their respective issue tracker systems."
msgstr ""

msgid "Java 11 deprecated"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The OpenJDK community will end active support for Java 11 in September 2023. "
"We still plan to support Java 11 past that date for core Quarkus "
"functionality, but Java 11 is now marked as deprecated. We recommend that "
"you upgrade to Java 17 or later if you want to use the latest and greatest "
"version of Quarkus."
msgstr ""

msgid "Release cadence and Long Term Support"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With Quarkus 3 finally out, we will be returning to our regular, continuous "
"cadence of releasing approximately every five weeks. This provides a "
"delivery train of small incremental changes that are easy to adopt and "
"upgrade to."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We do know some of you are looking for a more stable release cadence, and we "
"are working on a new long-term support (LTS) policy starting from Quarkus 3."
"2. We will provide details on this as we get closer to the 3.2 release. Java "
"11 will still be supported there for the core part of Quarkus."
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkiverse"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus is not just the https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus repository and "
"the Quarkus platform. It is also the whole rest of the Quarkus ecosystem - "
"the so-called Quarkiverse. Those extensions are hosted and maintained by "
"lots of contributors and organizations around the world. Some host these "
"extensions in their GitHub repositories, and others host them in the https://"
"github.com/quarkiverse[Quarkiverse Hub]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With Quarkus 3, due mainly to the package changes in many of the core "
"dependencies, we are happy to say that lots of those extensions have already "
"been updated to work with Quarkus 3.0.\n"
"We are working with the maintainers of the remaining extensions to get them "
"updated as well."
msgstr ""

msgid "Updating to Quarkus 3.0"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As usual, we wrote a https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-"
"Guide-3.0[very comprehensive migration guide] to help you update to Quarkus "
"3.0."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is complemented by a dedicated https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/"
"Migration-Guide-3.0:-Hibernate-ORM-5-to-6-migration[Hibernate ORM 6.2 update "
"guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"But that is not all:\n"
"Quarkus 3.0 introduces an update tool that can help you update your projects "
"to Quarkus 3."
msgstr ""

msgid "This upgrade tool will, among other tasks:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Update the Quarkus version"
msgstr ""

msgid "Adjust the packages to use the `jakarta.*` packages"
msgstr ""

msgid "Adjust your dependencies in some cases"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Upgrade your Quarkiverse extensions to versions compatible with Quarkus 3.0"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Adjust your configuration files when configuration properties have changed"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It doesn't handle everything (typically, Hibernate ORM API changes are not "
"covered by the update tool)\n"
"but it should handle most of the tedious work."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This update tool can be used for both Quarkus applications and Quarkus "
"extensions,\n"
"be they Maven or Gradle projects using Java or Kotlin."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are using the Quarkus CLI - which is recommended - upgrade it to the "
"latest and run:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are not using the CLI and using Maven, use the Quarkus Maven plugin "
"to update your projects:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are not using the CLI and using Gradle, use the Quarkus Gradle plugin "
"to do so:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information, consult the link:/guides/update-quarkus[dedicated "
"guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "I use Quarkus 2.x, do I need to update right away?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We are aware that the update to Quarkus 3.0 will require some work and "
"testing on your side, especially if you are using Hibernate ORM."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"That's why we will maintain Quarkus 2.16 with bugfixes and important CVE "
"fixes for a few months\n"
"so that you have the time to upgrade your applications to Quarkus 3.x."
msgstr ""

msgid "Full changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid "You can get the full changelog of Quarkus 3.0 on GitHub:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"3.0.0.Alpha1 and 3.0.0.Alpha2 changelogs are empty as these versions were "
"just a transformation of Quarkus 2 versions to Jakarta EE 10"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
